1
00:00:00,547 --> 00:00:02,547
♪

2
00:00:02,547 --> 00:00:04,927
( birds chirping )

3
00:00:04,927 --> 00:00:07,427
( bell tolls )

4
00:00:10,517 --> 00:00:12,437
( Kirito breathing heavily )

5
00:00:14,187 --> 00:00:16,857
( groans )

6
00:00:16,857 --> 00:00:18,647
JUST TEN MORE MINUTES.

7
00:00:18,647 --> 00:00:20,907
MAYBE FIVE.

8
00:00:20,907 --> 00:00:22,777
Selka: WAKE UP. NOW.

9
00:00:22,777 --> 00:00:25,867
( Kirito groans )

10
00:00:27,657 --> 00:00:29,617
SUGU?

11
00:00:29,617 --> 00:00:30,617
( Selka grunts )

12
00:00:35,417 --> 00:00:36,417
( Kirito gasps )

13
00:00:36,417 --> 00:00:37,877
Selka: WOULD YOU GET UP ALREADY?

14
00:00:37,877 --> 00:00:39,757
IT’S 5:30.

15
00:00:39,757 --> 00:00:43,137
EVEN THOUGH YOU’RE A LOST
CHILD OF VECTA AND A GUEST,

16
00:00:43,137 --> 00:00:45,217
YOU’RE STILL EXPECTED
TO GET UP ON TIME.

17
00:00:47,597 --> 00:00:48,597
Kirito: OKAY.

18
00:00:48,597 --> 00:00:50,307
Selka: HMPH.

19
00:00:50,307 --> 00:00:51,397
♪

20
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:28,067
( ax chops )

21
00:02:28,067 --> 00:02:30,657
Eugeo: 45!

22
00:02:30,657 --> 00:02:32,487
( ax rings )

23
00:02:35,617 --> 00:02:38,457
Kirito: THERE’S A LOT I DON’T
UNDERSTAND ABOUT THIS PLACE.

24
00:02:38,457 --> 00:02:41,127
BUT I KNOW
I’M GONNA NEED EUGEO’S HELP

25
00:02:41,127 --> 00:02:43,037
TO GET TO CENTORIA.

26
00:02:43,037 --> 00:02:47,127
THING IS, I HAVE TO GET HIM
OUT OF HIS CALLING FIRST,

27
00:02:47,127 --> 00:02:50,217
AND TO DO THAT, WE’LL HAVE
TO CHOP THIS TREE DOWN.

28
00:02:50,217 --> 00:02:53,177
- ( Eugeo sighs ) WHAT WAS THAT?
- Kirito: HUH? OH, NOTHING.

29
00:02:53,177 --> 00:02:55,307
Eugeo: WE’RE ALL DONE
WITH THE MORNING’S QUOTA.

30
00:02:55,307 --> 00:02:56,427
IT’S TIME FOR LUNCH.

31
00:02:58,307 --> 00:02:59,847
Kirito: I’M STARVING.

32
00:03:00,937 --> 00:03:03,307
( winces )

33
00:03:03,307 --> 00:03:05,017
Eugeo: KNOW WHAT I WISH?

34
00:03:05,017 --> 00:03:07,527
I WISH YOU COULD HAVE
TASTED THE PIES ALICE MADE.

35
00:03:07,527 --> 00:03:11,567
THE CRUST WAS SO FLAKY,
AND THERE WAS SO MUCH FILLING.

36
00:03:11,567 --> 00:03:14,327
HAVING IT WITH SOME FRESH MILK
WAS THE BEST.

37
00:03:14,327 --> 00:03:17,497
THERE’S NOTHING IN THE WORLD
THAT TASTED BETTER THAN THAT.

38
00:03:17,497 --> 00:03:20,247
Kirito: WAS THAT
ALICE’S CALLING, A BAKER?

39
00:03:20,247 --> 00:03:22,287
( Eugeo laughs ) NO, NOT EVEN!

40
00:03:22,287 --> 00:03:23,917
BACK IN THOSE DAYS,

41
00:03:23,917 --> 00:03:26,587
SHE WAS STUDYING THE SACRED ARTS
AT THE CHURCH.

42
00:03:26,587 --> 00:03:29,217
SHE WAS THE GREATEST PRODIGY
THIS VILLAGE EVER HAD.

43
00:03:29,217 --> 00:03:32,337
SHE COULD CAST ALL KINDS OF
SPELLS BY THE TIME SHE WAS TEN.

44
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:35,007
Kirito: WOW.

45
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:38,267
WHAT’S UP WITH THE GIRL LIVING
AT THE CHURCH, YOU KNOW, SELKA?

46
00:03:38,267 --> 00:03:41,387
Eugeo: OH, SHE’S ALICE’S
LITTLE SISTER.

47
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:44,607
AFTER ALICE WAS TAKEN AWAY,
SELKA MOVED TO THE CHURCH

48
00:03:44,607 --> 00:03:47,017
TO BECOME A NUN
AND STUDY THE SACRED ARTS.

49
00:03:47,017 --> 00:03:49,107
Kirito: OH.

50
00:03:49,107 --> 00:03:51,277
THERE’S A BUNCH OF KIDS
THERE, TOO.

51
00:03:51,277 --> 00:03:53,487
ARE THEY THERE
FOR THE SAME REASON AS HER?

52
00:03:53,487 --> 00:03:54,867
Eugeo: THEY LOST THEIR PARENTS

53
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:57,617
TO THE PLAGUE THAT HIT
THE VILLAGE THREE YEARS AGO.

54
00:03:57,617 --> 00:04:00,327
THE CHURCH IS THE ONLY PLACE
THAT HAD ROOM FOR THEM.

55
00:04:00,327 --> 00:04:01,577
POOR KIDS.

56
00:04:01,577 --> 00:04:03,997
IT’S LIKE WE’RE CURSED.

57
00:04:03,997 --> 00:04:07,247
ALL THESE STRANGE THINGS
HAVE BEEN HAPPENING LATELY,

58
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:10,297
LIKE PEOPLE BEING ATTACKED AND
KIDNAPPED DOWN THE MAIN ROAD.

59
00:04:10,297 --> 00:04:12,927
THE VILLAGERS SAY GOBLINS
ARE THE ONES DOING IT.

60
00:04:12,927 --> 00:04:14,507
Kirito: THERE’S GOBLINS HERE?

61
00:04:14,507 --> 00:04:17,847
Eugeo: I HAVE A FEELING
ALL THAT TALK’S JUST RUMORS.

62
00:04:17,847 --> 00:04:20,267
IF IT WERE TRUE,
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT

63
00:04:20,267 --> 00:04:22,477
SHOULD HAVE COME BY NOW
TO PUT A STOP TO THEM.

64
00:04:22,477 --> 00:04:24,687
THEY’D HAVE
BEEN HERE IN A FLASH,

65
00:04:24,687 --> 00:04:26,977
LIKE WHEN ALICE
TOUCHED THE GROUND

66
00:04:26,977 --> 00:04:28,357
IN THE DARK TERRITORY.

67
00:04:28,357 --> 00:04:31,187
THAT WAS NOTHING
COMPARED TO GOBLINS.

68
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:32,647
Kirito: NO, IT’S NOT.

69
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:35,527
Eugeo: EITHER WAY,
THERE HAVE BEEN A LOT OF DEATHS

70
00:04:35,527 --> 00:04:38,327
OVER THE PAST TWO OR
THREE YEARS, MORE THAN USUAL.

71
00:04:38,327 --> 00:04:40,237
Kirito: CAN’T YOU REVIVE ’EM?

72
00:04:40,237 --> 00:04:42,287
YOU KNOW, LIKE WITH ONE
OF THE SACRED ARTS?

73
00:04:42,287 --> 00:04:44,327
Eugeo: WELL...

74
00:04:44,327 --> 00:04:46,327
I DON’T KNOW ABOUT THAT,

75
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:47,917
BUT I REMEMBER ALICE SAYING

76
00:04:47,917 --> 00:04:49,497
THERE WAS
A HIGH-LEVEL SACRED ART

77
00:04:49,497 --> 00:04:51,257
THAT COULD STOP A LIFE
FROM DECREASING.

78
00:04:51,257 --> 00:04:54,217
Kirito: THAT’D BE
A GOOD ONE TO KNOW, I GUESS.

79
00:04:54,217 --> 00:04:56,007
Eugeo: IT WOULD.

80
00:04:56,007 --> 00:04:58,257
ALICE SAID SHE FOUND
A PASSAGE ABOUT THAT SPELL

81
00:04:58,257 --> 00:05:00,217
IN ONE OF THE OLD BOOKS
IN THE CHURCH.

82
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:02,017
BUT THE PROBLEM IS,

83
00:05:02,017 --> 00:05:04,477
ONLY THE HIGH PRIESTS
AT THE AXIOM CHURCH CAN USE IT.

84
00:05:04,477 --> 00:05:06,187
Kirito: AXIOM CHURCH?

85
00:05:06,187 --> 00:05:07,397
Eugeo: IT’S IN CENTORIA.

86
00:05:07,397 --> 00:05:09,187
THEY WROTE THE TABOO INDEX.

87
00:05:09,187 --> 00:05:10,937
Kirito: BUT, LIKE,
DO YOU HAVE TO BE

88
00:05:10,937 --> 00:05:12,777
A HIGH PRIEST TO USE THE SPELL?

89
00:05:12,777 --> 00:05:14,357
MAYBE SOMEONE LIKE YOU OR ME
COULD LEARN IT.

90
00:05:16,947 --> 00:05:18,197
Eugeo: NO.

91
00:05:18,197 --> 00:05:20,027
IT’S NOT
FOR REGULAR FOLK LIKE US.

92
00:05:20,027 --> 00:05:22,787
THE ARTS GET THEIR STRENGTH
FROM THE SACRED POWER

93
00:05:22,787 --> 00:05:26,537
THAT SOLUS AND TERRARIA
SATURATE THE AIR AND LAND WITH.

94
00:05:26,537 --> 00:05:30,747
THE MORE ELABORATE THE ART,
THE MORE SACRED POWER IT TAKES.

95
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:33,297
IT WOULD TAKE MORE POWER
THAN THIS FOREST HAS,

96
00:05:33,297 --> 00:05:35,377
AND NO ONE FROM HERE
TO ZAKKARIA COULD WIELD IT.

97
00:05:37,507 --> 00:05:38,757
Kirito: THAT’S TOO BAD.

98
00:05:38,757 --> 00:05:40,507
I WONDER IF THERE’S A SACRED ART

99
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,387
THAT COULD HELP US
TO CHOP THIS THING DOWN.

100
00:05:42,387 --> 00:05:43,887
( Eugeo laughs )

101
00:05:43,887 --> 00:05:45,677
THAT WOULD MAKE THINGS EASIER!

102
00:05:45,677 --> 00:05:49,057
Kirito: THERE’S GOTTA BE
SOMETHING BETTER THAN THIS.

103
00:05:49,057 --> 00:05:50,267
( gasps )

104
00:05:51,357 --> 00:05:53,357
HEY, EUGEO,

105
00:05:53,357 --> 00:05:55,357
IS THERE ANYTHING TOUGHER
THAN THIS IN YOUR VILLAGE?

106
00:05:55,357 --> 00:05:57,107
Eugeo: NO, I’M AFRAID NOT.

107
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:59,617
THE ONLY THING STRONGER
THAN THE DRAGONBONE AX

108
00:05:59,617 --> 00:06:01,077
WOULD BE AN INTEGRITY KNI--

109
00:06:01,077 --> 00:06:02,787
( sighs )

110
00:06:02,787 --> 00:06:05,037
ON SECOND THOUGHT,
MAYBE THERE IS.

111
00:06:06,707 --> 00:06:08,577
WAIT HERE FOR ME.
I’LL BE BACK IN A BIT.

112
00:06:08,577 --> 00:06:10,037
Kirito: HUH?

113
00:06:10,037 --> 00:06:11,957
♪

114
00:06:14,257 --> 00:06:15,837
( Eugeo panting )

115
00:06:18,927 --> 00:06:20,587
- ( grunts )
- Kirito: WHOA.

116
00:06:20,587 --> 00:06:21,967
YOU OKAY?

117
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:23,467
( Eugeo panting )

118
00:06:25,557 --> 00:06:27,887
Kirito: MIND IF I OPEN IT?

119
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:30,267
Eugeo: OKAY. JUST BE CAREFUL.

120
00:06:30,267 --> 00:06:31,857
IF IT FALLS ON YOUR FOOT,

121
00:06:31,857 --> 00:06:33,977
IT’LL LEAVE YOU
WITH MORE THAN A SCRATCH.

122
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:35,147
( Kirito gasps )

123
00:06:35,147 --> 00:06:38,237
( grunting )

124
00:06:38,237 --> 00:06:38,897
WHEW.

125
00:06:45,327 --> 00:06:46,497
( gasps )

126
00:06:46,497 --> 00:06:49,247
♪

127
00:06:49,247 --> 00:06:50,957
( gasps )

128
00:06:50,957 --> 00:06:53,287
NO WAY.

129
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:56,337
Eugeo: IT’S THE BLUE ROSE SWORD
FROM THE FAIRY TALE.

130
00:06:56,337 --> 00:06:57,507
Kirito: WHAT FAIRY TALE?

131
00:06:57,507 --> 00:06:59,167
Eugeo: IT GOES LIKE THIS.

132
00:06:59,167 --> 00:07:01,637
300 YEARS AGO,
BERCOULI THE SWORDSMAN

133
00:07:01,637 --> 00:07:03,297
WENT TO THE END MOUNTAINS.

134
00:07:03,297 --> 00:07:06,467
HE ENTERED THE LAIR OF
THE WHITE DRAGON, OUR PROTECTOR,

135
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:08,557
AND FOUND THAT SWORD.

136
00:07:08,557 --> 00:07:11,267
IT’S JUST A SILLY STORY.

137
00:07:11,267 --> 00:07:14,267
THAT IS, IT WAS,

138
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,977
UNTIL SOME KIDS DECIDED
TO FIND OUT IF IT WAS TRUE.

139
00:07:16,977 --> 00:07:18,737
I MENTIONED IT YESTERDAY.

140
00:07:18,737 --> 00:07:23,237
REMEMBER? ABOUT HOW ALICE AND I
WENT TO THE END MOUNTAINS.

141
00:07:23,237 --> 00:07:25,827
I FOUND THAT SWORD
IN THE DRAGON’S LAIR.

142
00:07:25,827 --> 00:07:28,577
I COULDN’T EVEN LIFT IT
BY MYSELF BACK THEN.

143
00:07:28,577 --> 00:07:31,077
Kirito: REALLY?
WHAT’D THE DRAGON HAVE TO SAY

144
00:07:31,077 --> 00:07:32,787
ABOUT YOU GUYS
BREAKIN’ IN TO ITS HOME?

145
00:07:32,787 --> 00:07:35,667
Eugeo: OH, THERE WAS NOTHING
LEFT OF IT EXCEPT SOME BONES.

146
00:07:35,667 --> 00:07:37,337
WE TOOK THE WRONG TUNNEL,

147
00:07:37,337 --> 00:07:39,757
AND THEN ALICE CROSSED
INTO THE DARK TERRITORY.

148
00:07:42,547 --> 00:07:45,507
AND THEN SHE WAS TAKEN AWAY.

149
00:07:45,507 --> 00:07:48,677
I COULDN’T DO ANYTHING FOR HER,
EXCEPT STAND THERE.

150
00:07:48,677 --> 00:07:50,517
I WANTED TO SAVE HER,

151
00:07:50,517 --> 00:07:53,227
BUT MY ARMS AND LEGS
WERE FROZEN.

152
00:07:53,227 --> 00:07:56,567
I-I’M SORRY. BACK TO THE SWORD.

153
00:07:56,567 --> 00:08:00,187
I LEFT IT THERE THAT DAY
AND NEVER FORGOT IT,

154
00:08:00,187 --> 00:08:02,567
SO TWO SUMMERS AGO,
I WENT BACK.

155
00:08:02,567 --> 00:08:04,657
EVERY DAY OF REST,
I’D GO DRAG IT.

156
00:08:04,657 --> 00:08:06,907
IT TOOK THREE MONTHS
TO GET IT BACK HERE.

157
00:08:06,907 --> 00:08:09,577
Kirito: IT TOOK YOU
THREE WHOLE MONTHS TO DO IT?

158
00:08:09,577 --> 00:08:11,497
WHY’D YOU EVEN BOTHER?

159
00:08:11,497 --> 00:08:13,367
Eugeo: I GUESS I WAS HOPING

160
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:16,087
ONE DAY I’D HAVE
THE STRENGTH TO SWING IT.

161
00:08:16,087 --> 00:08:18,457
I’M STILL NOT STRONG ENOUGH TO.

162
00:08:18,457 --> 00:08:19,707
DO YOU THINK YOU ARE?

163
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:21,297
Kirito: I’M DOWN TO TRY.

164
00:08:21,297 --> 00:08:22,797
I’M A SWORDSMAN, AFTER ALL.

165
00:08:24,387 --> 00:08:25,257
( hand scraping )

166
00:08:25,257 --> 00:08:27,047
( grunting )

167
00:08:27,047 --> 00:08:28,557
( blade rings )

168
00:08:28,557 --> 00:08:30,347
WHOA! UNH!

169
00:08:30,347 --> 00:08:31,227
( blade clangs )

170
00:08:31,227 --> 00:08:32,557
( sighs )

171
00:08:32,557 --> 00:08:33,887
( Eugeo chuckles )

172
00:08:33,887 --> 00:08:36,357
LOOKS LIKE IT’S
TOO HEAVY FOR YOU, TOO.

173
00:08:36,357 --> 00:08:37,767
( blade rings )

174
00:08:37,767 --> 00:08:40,687
Kirito: IT’S NOT MADE OF STEEL.
OR IS IT?

175
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,487
Eugeo: NO, I DON’T THINK SO.

176
00:08:42,487 --> 00:08:44,857
AND IT’S NOT SILVER
OR DRAGONBONE, EITHER.

177
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:47,027
I THINK IT MIGHT BE
A DIVINE OBJECT.

178
00:08:47,027 --> 00:08:48,407
Kirito: A WHAT?

179
00:08:48,407 --> 00:08:50,657
Eugeo: IT’S SOMETHING
THAT WAS EITHER MADE

180
00:08:50,657 --> 00:08:54,367
WITH THE HELP OF THE GODS
OR WAS CREATED BY THEM.

181
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:57,077
WE CALL THINGS LIKE THAT
DIVINE OBJECTS.

182
00:08:57,077 --> 00:08:58,497
Kirito: THAT MAKES SENSE.

183
00:08:58,497 --> 00:09:00,707
HEY, EUGEO? COULD YOU, LIKE,

184
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:02,917
CHECK HOW MUCH LIFE
THE GIGAS CEDAR HAS NOW?

185
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:04,627
Eugeo: DON’T TELL ME.
LET ME GUESS.

186
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,137
YOU’RE GOING TO TRY
STRIKING IT WITH THE SWORD.

187
00:09:07,137 --> 00:09:09,097
Kirito:
YOU’RE DAMN STRAIGHT, I AM.

188
00:09:09,097 --> 00:09:11,137
UNLESS THE TABOO INDEX
FORBIDS IT,

189
00:09:11,137 --> 00:09:12,727
BUT I BET IT DOESN’T, DOES IT?

190
00:09:12,727 --> 00:09:14,557
( Eugeo chuckles )
NO, IT DOESN’T.

191
00:09:14,557 --> 00:09:17,307
IT’S FUNNY.
ALL THIS SEEMS SO FAMILIAR.

192
00:09:22,067 --> 00:09:26,817
RIGHT NOW, IT’S AT 232,315.

193
00:09:26,817 --> 00:09:28,657
Kirito: COOL. REMEMBER THAT.

194
00:09:28,657 --> 00:09:29,657
( hands scraping )

195
00:09:29,657 --> 00:09:31,577
( grunts )

196
00:09:33,537 --> 00:09:35,707
( deep breath )

197
00:09:40,247 --> 00:09:41,337
( yells )

198
00:09:41,337 --> 00:09:44,507
( blade rings )

199
00:09:46,087 --> 00:09:48,427
( grunts )

200
00:09:48,427 --> 00:09:50,177
Eugeo: DID YOU HURT YOURSELF?!

201
00:09:50,177 --> 00:09:52,637
Kirito: NO, I’M OKAY.

202
00:09:52,637 --> 00:09:55,427
Eugeo: I TOLD YOU BEFORE.
THAT TREE IS TOUGH.

203
00:09:55,427 --> 00:09:56,347
( gasps )

204
00:09:58,187 --> 00:10:01,397
NO WAY.
YOU ACTUALLY CUT INTO IT.

205
00:10:04,737 --> 00:10:07,027
AND DEEP, TOO.

206
00:10:07,027 --> 00:10:09,567
Kirito: GO ON.
SEE WHERE ITS LIFE’S AT NOW.

207
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,867
Eugeo: OH. RIGHT.

208
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,697
232,314.

209
00:10:15,697 --> 00:10:17,407
Kirito: YOU’RE KIDDING!

210
00:10:17,407 --> 00:10:19,747
IT ONLY WENT DOWN ONE POINT?!

211
00:10:19,747 --> 00:10:21,917
Eugeo: YOUR HIT LANDED
IN THE WRONG SPOT.

212
00:10:21,917 --> 00:10:24,877
I BET IT WOULD HAVE
DECREASED ITS LIFE A LOT MORE

213
00:10:24,877 --> 00:10:27,877
IF YOU GOT IT IN THE CENTER
OF THE CUT INSTEAD OF THE BARK.

214
00:10:27,877 --> 00:10:30,507
LOOKS LIKE
YOUR INTUITION WAS RIGHT.

215
00:10:30,507 --> 00:10:32,927
THE SWORD IS
MORE EFFECTIVE THAN THE AX.

216
00:10:32,927 --> 00:10:37,477
EVEN SO, WE’D HAVE TO MASTER
USING IT TO GET ANY RESULTS.

217
00:10:37,477 --> 00:10:39,847
Kirito: I CAN’T HIT IT STRAIGHT,
BUT I BET YOU COULD.

218
00:10:39,847 --> 00:10:42,767
Eugeo: I CAN BARELY HOLD
THE SWORD, LET ALONE SWING IT.

219
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:44,317
Kirito: IT’S ALL
ABOUT TECHNIQUE,

220
00:10:44,317 --> 00:10:45,477
AND I CAN HELP YOU WITH THAT.

221
00:10:45,477 --> 00:10:47,687
( Eugeo sighs )

222
00:10:47,687 --> 00:10:49,447
OKAY, I’LL GIVE IT A SHOT.

223
00:10:51,527 --> 00:10:53,447
( grunting )

224
00:10:55,577 --> 00:10:57,747
S-SO HEAVY!

225
00:10:57,747 --> 00:10:59,537
Kirito: FIRST THING,
FIND YOUR BALANCE,

226
00:10:59,537 --> 00:11:01,457
AND WHEN YOU SWING,
SWING WITH YOUR BODY.

227
00:11:01,457 --> 00:11:03,167
WITH SWORDS,
IT’S MORE ABOUT MOMENTUM,

228
00:11:03,167 --> 00:11:04,457
NOT JUST ARM STRENGTH.

229
00:11:04,457 --> 00:11:05,297
Eugeo: MM-HMM.

230
00:11:09,087 --> 00:11:11,427
- ( hands scraping )
- ( deep breath )

231
00:11:19,517 --> 00:11:20,517
Kirito: WHOA!

232
00:11:20,517 --> 00:11:22,437
( blade rings )

233
00:11:22,437 --> 00:11:24,147
( Eugeo grunting )

234
00:11:26,857 --> 00:11:28,397
Kirito: HEY! YOU ALL RIGHT?

235
00:11:28,397 --> 00:11:30,897
Eugeo: I THINK
I LOST SOME LIFE ON THAT ONE.

236
00:11:30,897 --> 00:11:33,447
Kirito: OH, WELL.
IT WAS A GOOD TRY.

237
00:11:37,537 --> 00:11:40,117
( gasps )

238
00:11:42,077 --> 00:11:46,707
IF DURABILITY’S LIFE,
I LOST SOME WHEN I TOOK A SWING.

239
00:11:46,707 --> 00:11:50,797
HMM. IT SAYS MY OBJECT CONTROL
AUTHORITY’S AT 38.

240
00:11:50,797 --> 00:11:52,427
I GUESS THAT’S MY PARAMETER.

241
00:11:56,887 --> 00:11:58,597
THE SWORD’S IS HIGHER.

242
00:12:00,057 --> 00:12:02,897
- ( water splashes )
- ( sighs )

243
00:12:02,897 --> 00:12:04,857
THAT’S WHAT I’M TALKIN’ ABOUT.

244
00:12:04,857 --> 00:12:07,477
( deep breath )

245
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:10,817
AT THIS RATE,
I’LL NEVER GET TO CENTORIA.

246
00:12:10,817 --> 00:12:14,657
I NEED EUGEO’S HELP, BUT HE
WON’T BAIL ON HIS CALLING.

247
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:18,487
IF IT WASN’T
FOR THAT TABOO INDEX,

248
00:12:18,487 --> 00:12:20,497
HE COULD DO WHATEVER HE WANTS.

249
00:12:20,497 --> 00:12:23,667
HE SAID THE AXIOM CHURCH
CAME UP WITH IT.

250
00:12:23,667 --> 00:12:25,827
WONDER WHAT THE DEAL IS
WITH THEM.

251
00:12:25,827 --> 00:12:28,917
IF I’M RIGHT AND THESE PEOPLE
ARE A.I. FLUCTLIGHTS

252
00:12:28,917 --> 00:12:30,917
IN A SIMULATED CIVILIZATION,

253
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:34,007
THERE’S NO WAY THE SYSTEM
WOULD LET ’EM BREAK A RULE.

254
00:12:35,507 --> 00:12:36,967
HANG ON.

255
00:12:36,967 --> 00:12:39,717
EUGEO SAID ALICE
BROKE THE TABOO INDEX

256
00:12:39,717 --> 00:12:42,767
WHEN SHE ACCIDENTALLY
CROSSED INTO THE DARK TERRITORY,

257
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:45,647
BUT SHE WAS THERE BY CHOICE.

258
00:12:45,647 --> 00:12:47,937
SHE WENT AGAINST THE SYSTEM.

259
00:12:47,937 --> 00:12:50,857
SO IS SHE NOT AN A.I.?

260
00:12:50,857 --> 00:12:52,817
Selka: HELLO?
IS SOMEONE IN THERE?

261
00:12:52,817 --> 00:12:54,447
Kirito: Y-YEAH, THERE IS!

262
00:12:54,447 --> 00:12:55,777
I-I’M ALMOST DONE!

263
00:12:55,777 --> 00:12:59,447
Selka: OH! UM, NO.
YOU CAN TAKE YOUR TIME.

264
00:12:59,447 --> 00:13:00,827
I WAS JUST CHECKING.

265
00:13:00,827 --> 00:13:02,787
SORRY TO BOTHER YOU.
GOOD NIGHT.

266
00:13:02,787 --> 00:13:04,667
Kirito: UH, SELKA!

267
00:13:04,667 --> 00:13:06,377
I WANTED TO ASK YOU SOMETHING.

268
00:13:06,377 --> 00:13:07,457
Selka: MM...

269
00:13:09,337 --> 00:13:11,257
♪

270
00:13:13,877 --> 00:13:15,177
- ( knock on door )
- MM?

271
00:13:17,257 --> 00:13:19,887
Selka: SO? WHAT WAS IT
YOU WANTED TO ASK ME?

272
00:13:19,887 --> 00:13:21,097
Kirito: YEAH.

273
00:13:23,927 --> 00:13:25,307
UM...

274
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:28,727
IT’S ABOUT YOUR OLDER SISTER.

275
00:13:28,727 --> 00:13:30,357
( Selka gasps )

276
00:13:30,357 --> 00:13:31,937
Kirito: I HEARD ABOUT HER,

277
00:13:31,937 --> 00:13:33,687
YOU KNOW, FROM EUGEO.

278
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:36,817
AND, LIKE, HE TOLD ME
HER NAME WAS ALICE.

279
00:13:36,817 --> 00:13:38,697
Selka: HE DID, DID HE?

280
00:13:38,697 --> 00:13:41,737
WHAT ELSE DID HE TELL YOU,
BESIDES HER NAME WAS ALICE?

281
00:13:41,737 --> 00:13:44,447
Kirito: OH, UM,
HE SAID SHE WAS STUDYING

282
00:13:44,447 --> 00:13:46,577
THE SACRED ARTS
HERE AT THE CHURCH

283
00:13:46,577 --> 00:13:49,747
AND HOW, SIX YEARS AGO,
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT TOOK HER.

284
00:13:49,747 --> 00:13:52,167
I GOT THE FEELING
HE’S REALLY WORRIED ABOUT HER.

285
00:13:52,167 --> 00:13:57,377
Selka: I DIDN’T KNOW.
I THOUGHT HE FORGOT ABOUT HER.

286
00:13:57,377 --> 00:13:59,927
THIS EXPLAINS A LOT
ABOUT HIM, THOUGH.

287
00:13:59,927 --> 00:14:02,257
SHE’S THE REASON EUGEO’S SO SAD.

288
00:14:02,257 --> 00:14:04,977
Kirito: I DIDN’T GET THAT.
HE SEEMS FINE.

289
00:14:04,977 --> 00:14:07,807
Selka: HE’S NOT.
YOU HAD TO HAVE NOTICED IT,

290
00:14:07,807 --> 00:14:09,807
HOW QUIET AND GLOOMY HE IS.

291
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,897
Kirito: OH. YEAH.

292
00:14:11,897 --> 00:14:13,937
Selka: WHEN MY SISTER WAS HERE,

293
00:14:13,937 --> 00:14:17,277
EVERY TIME I SAW HIM,
HE HAD A SMILE ON HIS FACE.

294
00:14:17,277 --> 00:14:21,027
I DON’T REMEMBER EVER SEEING HIM
WITHOUT ONE BACK THEN.

295
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:25,827
BUT NOT ANY MORE. HE SPENDS
HIS DAYS OF REST ALONE,

296
00:14:25,827 --> 00:14:28,167
AND THE ONLY TIME I SEE HIM
IS WHEN HE GOES TO THE FOREST.

297
00:14:29,787 --> 00:14:31,247
Kirito: SELKA...

298
00:14:31,247 --> 00:14:32,627
YOU REALLY LIKE HIM, DON’T YOU?

299
00:14:32,627 --> 00:14:33,917
( Selka squeals )

300
00:14:33,917 --> 00:14:36,467
I DIDN’T SAY THAT! OH, MY GOSH!

301
00:14:36,467 --> 00:14:38,007
( Kirito laughs )

302
00:14:39,627 --> 00:14:41,547
Selka: EVERYONE
COMPARES ME TO ALICE.

303
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,427
NO ONE SAYS IT, BUT I KNOW.

304
00:14:43,427 --> 00:14:47,267
WHEN MY PARENTS SEE ME,
I REMIND THEM OF HER,

305
00:14:47,267 --> 00:14:49,267
AND I CAN’T STAND IT ANY MORE.

306
00:14:49,267 --> 00:14:52,557
THAT’S PROBABLY
WHY EUGEO AVOIDS ME.

307
00:14:52,557 --> 00:14:54,977
WHEN HE SEES ME,
HE THINKS OF HER,

308
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:57,237
AND I CAN TELL
IT MAKES HIM SAD.

309
00:14:57,237 --> 00:15:00,697
BUT THERE’S NOTHING I CAN DO.

310
00:15:00,697 --> 00:15:02,567
IT’S NOT MY FAULT SHE’S GONE.

311
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:06,537
( gasps )

312
00:15:06,537 --> 00:15:08,957
I’M SORRY.
I’M ACTING LIKE A BABY.

313
00:15:08,957 --> 00:15:10,997
Kirito: NO, NOT AT ALL.

314
00:15:10,997 --> 00:15:12,957
IT’S GOOD TO CRY.

315
00:15:12,957 --> 00:15:15,047
IT’S BETTER THAN HOLDIN’ IT IN.

316
00:15:15,047 --> 00:15:17,667
Selka: YES, YOU’RE RIGHT.

317
00:15:17,667 --> 00:15:20,627
IN FACT, I FEEL
MUCH BETTER ALREADY.

318
00:15:20,627 --> 00:15:22,637
CRYING IN FRONT OF OTHERS IS...

319
00:15:22,637 --> 00:15:24,007
NOT SOMETHING I DO.

320
00:15:24,007 --> 00:15:27,267
Kirito: REALLY?
YOU’RE TOUGHER THAN I AM.

321
00:15:27,267 --> 00:15:30,637
I CAN’T TELL YOU HOW MANY TIMES
I’VE CRIED IN FRONT OF PEOPLE.

322
00:15:32,147 --> 00:15:34,687
Selka: HOLD ON.
IS YOUR MEMORY BACK?

323
00:15:34,687 --> 00:15:37,067
Kirito: NO! I-IT JUST
FEELS THAT WAY, IS ALL!

324
00:15:37,067 --> 00:15:39,187
A-ANYWAY, BACK TO YOU.

325
00:15:39,187 --> 00:15:41,277
IT DOESN’T MATTER
WHAT ANYONE THINKS.

326
00:15:41,277 --> 00:15:43,407
YOU’RE YOU, NOT YOUR SISTER.

327
00:15:43,407 --> 00:15:47,287
YOU CAN ONLY LIVE YOUR LIFE,
NOT SOMEONE ELSE’S.

328
00:15:47,287 --> 00:15:49,037
( Selka chuckles )
YES, YOU’RE RIGHT.

329
00:15:49,037 --> 00:15:50,707
- ( bell tolling )
- ( gasps )

330
00:15:52,957 --> 00:15:54,417
I SHOULD GET GOING.

331
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:57,497
SAY...

332
00:15:57,497 --> 00:15:59,627
DID EUGEO HAPPEN TO TELL YOU

333
00:15:59,627 --> 00:16:02,547
WHY THE INTEGRITY KNIGHT
TOOK MY SISTER AWAY?

334
00:16:02,547 --> 00:16:04,637
Kirito: UM, YEAH. HE DID.

335
00:16:04,637 --> 00:16:06,717
Selka: MY PARENTS
WOULDN’T TELL ME,

336
00:16:06,717 --> 00:16:09,267
AND EUGEO
WOULDN’T TELL ME, EITHER.

337
00:16:09,267 --> 00:16:11,597
MAYBE YOU COULD TELL ME WHY?

338
00:16:11,597 --> 00:16:15,057
Kirito: YEAH, SURE.
SHE WENT TO THE END MOUNTAINS,

339
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:19,027
THEN TOUCHED THE GROUND
ON THE DARK TERRITORY SIDE.

340
00:16:19,027 --> 00:16:21,947
Selka: I SEE.
THE END MOUNTAINS, HUH?

341
00:16:21,947 --> 00:16:23,027
Kirito: UH...

342
00:16:25,117 --> 00:16:26,987
Selka: TOMORROW IS
OUR DAY OF REST.

343
00:16:26,987 --> 00:16:28,447
STILL, BE ON TIME.

344
00:16:28,447 --> 00:16:30,497
I WON’T BE COMING
TO WAKE YOU UP ANY MORE.

345
00:16:30,497 --> 00:16:32,787
Kirito: OKAY.
I’LL KEEP THAT IN MIND.

346
00:16:35,207 --> 00:16:36,587
( door closes )

347
00:16:42,547 --> 00:16:44,467
( birds chirping )

348
00:16:46,847 --> 00:16:47,797
( sighs )

349
00:16:48,967 --> 00:16:50,717
Azalia: GOOD MORNING.

350
00:16:50,717 --> 00:16:53,307
Kirito: UH, OH, GOOD MORNING.

351
00:16:53,307 --> 00:16:56,397
Azalia: BY CHANCE,
HAVE YOU SEEN SELKA TODAY?

352
00:16:56,397 --> 00:16:58,817
Kirito: NO.
I JUST WOKE UP, ACTUALLY.

353
00:16:58,817 --> 00:17:03,027
Azalia: SO I SEE. WELL,
I HAVE NOT SEEN HER ALL MORNING.

354
00:17:03,027 --> 00:17:06,357
SHE MISSED PRAYERS,
AND SHE IS NOT IN HER ROOM.

355
00:17:06,357 --> 00:17:10,037
I AM WORRIED. SHE WOULD NEVER
LEAVE WITHOUT TELLING ME FIRST.

356
00:17:10,037 --> 00:17:11,867
Kirito: I’M SURE SHE’S AROUND.

357
00:17:11,867 --> 00:17:15,207
Azalia: I HOPE SO. IF YOU
SEE HER, PLEASE LET ME KNOW.

358
00:17:15,207 --> 00:17:16,457
Kirito: YES, MA’AM.

359
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,037
EUGEO!

360
00:17:19,037 --> 00:17:20,457
Eugeo: HEY, KIRITO.

361
00:17:20,457 --> 00:17:22,127
Kirito: HAVE YOU
SEEN SELKA ANYWHERE?

362
00:17:22,127 --> 00:17:24,127
Eugeo: I HAVEN’T. WHY?

363
00:17:24,127 --> 00:17:27,007
Kirito: SISTER AZALIA’S
BEEN LOOKING FOR HER.

364
00:17:27,007 --> 00:17:28,637
SHE SAYS SHE LEFT
WITHOUT TELLING HER.

365
00:17:28,637 --> 00:17:30,007
Eugeo: THAT’S STRANGE.

366
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,467
Kirito: WELL,
I’M TRYIN’ TO FIND HER.

367
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:32,887
DO YOU KNOW
WHERE SHE COULD’VE GONE?

368
00:17:32,887 --> 00:17:36,017
Eugeo: NO. SHE AND I
HAVEN’T SPOKEN IN AGES.

369
00:17:36,017 --> 00:17:38,097
DO YOU THINK SOMETHING
MIGHT HAVE UPSET HER?

370
00:17:38,097 --> 00:17:39,437
Kirito: UH...

371
00:17:40,767 --> 00:17:41,977
Selka: I SEE.

372
00:17:41,977 --> 00:17:43,817
THE END MOUNTAINS, HUH?

373
00:17:43,817 --> 00:17:45,817
Kirito: AW, MAN. LAST NIGHT,

374
00:17:45,817 --> 00:17:47,697
I TOLD HER
WHAT HAPPENED TO ALICE,

375
00:17:47,697 --> 00:17:49,777
AT LEAST, EVERYTHING
YOU TOLD ME THAT HAPPENED.

376
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:50,907
( Eugeo gasps )

377
00:17:50,907 --> 00:17:52,197
Kirito: SHE WOULDN’T GO

378
00:17:52,197 --> 00:17:54,787
TO THE END MOUNTAINS
ON HER OWN, WOULD SHE?

379
00:17:54,787 --> 00:17:56,827
Eugeo: THAT’S EXACTLY
WHERE SHE WENT!

380
00:17:56,827 --> 00:17:58,667
WE HAVE TO BRING HER BACK NOW!

381
00:18:06,797 --> 00:18:07,967
Kirito: WHAT’S WRONG?

382
00:18:07,967 --> 00:18:09,547
Eugeo: IT’S BEEN STEPPED ON.

383
00:18:13,137 --> 00:18:15,057
IT’S LOST A BIT OF LIFE.

384
00:18:15,057 --> 00:18:17,937
SOMEONE’S BEEN BY HERE,
AND IT WASN’T THAT LONG AGO.

385
00:18:17,937 --> 00:18:19,807
Kirito: THEN WE’RE
ON THE RIGHT TRACK.

386
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:21,057
- THAT’S GOTTA BE SELKA.
- Eugeo: YEAH.

387
00:18:26,817 --> 00:18:29,107
WELL, THIS IS IT.

388
00:18:30,237 --> 00:18:31,237
Kirito: NO WAY.

389
00:18:31,237 --> 00:18:33,987
IT REALLY IS THE END.

390
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:38,117
Eugeo: WHEN I FIRST CAME HERE,
I THOUGHT THE SAME THING.

391
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:41,837
Kirito: AND THE DARK TERRITORY’S
DOWN THAT WAY, HUH?

392
00:18:41,837 --> 00:18:43,037
Eugeo: YEAH. ARE YOU READY?

393
00:18:43,037 --> 00:18:45,297
Kirito: YEAH, I THINK. I GUESS.

394
00:18:45,297 --> 00:18:47,087
- Eugeo: SYSTEM CALL.
- ( Kirito gasps )

395
00:18:47,087 --> 00:18:49,757
Eugeo: GENERATE
LUMINOUS ELEMENT.

396
00:18:49,757 --> 00:18:52,137
ADHERE.

397
00:18:52,137 --> 00:18:54,387
Kirito: E-EUGEO! WHAT’D YOU DO?

398
00:18:54,387 --> 00:18:55,967
Eugeo: IT’S A SACRED ART,

399
00:18:55,967 --> 00:18:58,097
AN EASY ONE THAT ANYBODY CAN DO.

400
00:18:58,097 --> 00:19:00,187
Kirito: BUT, LIKE,
YOU SAID, "SYSTEM."

401
00:19:00,187 --> 00:19:01,607
DO YOU EVEN KNOW
WHAT THAT MEANS?

402
00:19:01,607 --> 00:19:03,937
Eugeo: NOTHING.
IT’S JUST A WORD,

403
00:19:03,937 --> 00:19:05,227
WELL, A COMMAND.

404
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,857
IT’S TO CALL ON THE GODS.

405
00:19:06,857 --> 00:19:08,487
AS LONG AS YOU HAVE
ENOUGH SKILL,

406
00:19:08,487 --> 00:19:10,277
YOU’LL BE BLESSED
WITH THE ART YOU SUMMON.

407
00:19:10,277 --> 00:19:13,237
Kirito: HE THINKS
HE’S CASTING A MAGIC SPELL.

408
00:19:13,237 --> 00:19:15,157
Eugeo: COME ON. LET’S GO.

409
00:19:15,157 --> 00:19:15,947
Kirito: RIGHT.

410
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:18,537
♪

411
00:19:21,627 --> 00:19:23,537
- ( breeze blowing )
- ( Kirito shivers )

412
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:25,627
MAYBE SHE DIDN’T COME IN HERE.

413
00:19:25,627 --> 00:19:27,167
I MEAN, THERE’S NO SIGN OF HER.

414
00:19:27,167 --> 00:19:28,797
( Eugeo gasps )

415
00:19:31,377 --> 00:19:33,887
THIS IS AS GOOD A SIGN AS ANY.

416
00:19:33,887 --> 00:19:35,467
Kirito:
IT COULD BE HER, I GUESS.

417
00:19:39,097 --> 00:19:40,887
HEY, EUGEO.

418
00:19:40,887 --> 00:19:42,267
Eugeo: WHAT IS IT?

419
00:19:42,267 --> 00:19:44,647
Kirito: IF SHE CROSSES
INTO THE DARK TERRITORY,

420
00:19:44,647 --> 00:19:47,277
DOES AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT COME
AND TAKE HER RIGHT AWAY?

421
00:19:47,277 --> 00:19:50,027
Eugeo: NO,
NOT UNTIL THE NEXT DAY.

422
00:19:50,027 --> 00:19:52,987
HE’LL FLY TO THE VILLAGE
AND ARREST HER THERE,

423
00:19:52,987 --> 00:19:54,487
JUST LIKE SIX YEARS AGO.

424
00:19:54,487 --> 00:19:56,947
Kirito: THEN,
EVEN IF WE’RE TOO LATE,

425
00:19:56,947 --> 00:19:59,157
WE STILL HAVE A CHANCE
TO KEEP HIM FROM GETTIN’ HER.

426
00:19:59,157 --> 00:20:00,457
( Eugeo sighs )

427
00:20:00,457 --> 00:20:02,167
BUT THAT WOULD BE INTERFERING.

428
00:20:02,167 --> 00:20:03,917
WE CAN’T.

429
00:20:03,917 --> 00:20:05,337
Kirito: OF COURSE WE CAN.

430
00:20:05,337 --> 00:20:08,127
LOOK, EVEN IF SHE DOES
BREAK THE TABOO INDEX,

431
00:20:08,127 --> 00:20:10,797
ALL WE HAVE TO DO IS
KEEP HER AWAY FROM THE VILLAGE.

432
00:20:10,797 --> 00:20:12,377
THE INTEGRITY KNIGHT
CAN’T ARREST HER

433
00:20:12,377 --> 00:20:13,387
IF HE CAN’T FIND HER.

434
00:20:13,387 --> 00:20:15,347
Eugeo: THAT’S INSANE.

435
00:20:15,347 --> 00:20:18,967
WE CAN’T HIDE FOREVER,
AND I HAVE MY CALLING.

436
00:20:18,967 --> 00:20:22,187
Kirito: BUT I DON’T,
SO I CAN TAKE HER AWAY.

437
00:20:22,187 --> 00:20:25,437
IF I DIDN’T SAY ANYTHING,
SHE WOULDN’T BE IN THIS MESS.

438
00:20:25,437 --> 00:20:27,017
THIS IS ALL ON ME.

439
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:29,027
Eugeo: NO, IT’S NOT.

440
00:20:29,027 --> 00:20:30,237
( Selka screams )

441
00:20:30,237 --> 00:20:31,697
Eugeo: SELKA!

442
00:20:34,947 --> 00:20:36,277
THAT WAY!

443
00:20:43,207 --> 00:20:44,667
Kirito: TAKE COVER.

444
00:20:52,127 --> 00:20:52,797
( gasps )

445
00:20:54,427 --> 00:20:56,177
( goblins laugh, chatter )

446
00:20:57,257 --> 00:20:58,387
( goblin growls )

447
00:20:59,847 --> 00:21:02,517
Kirito: CRAP. GOBLINS.

448
00:21:07,187 --> 00:21:08,857
( gasps )

449
00:21:08,857 --> 00:21:09,687
( Eugeo gasps )

450
00:21:11,777 --> 00:21:13,187
SELKA!

451
00:21:13,187 --> 00:21:15,447
Kirito: WHAT ARE YOU DOING?!

452
00:21:15,447 --> 00:21:17,407
( goblin growls )

453
00:21:17,407 --> 00:21:19,867
( goblins murmuring )

454
00:21:21,447 --> 00:21:24,247
Goblin #2: LOOKIE, LOOKIE!

455
00:21:24,247 --> 00:21:28,207
TWO MORE WHITE IUM BRATTY-BRATS,
JUST A-WANDERING AROUND!

456
00:21:28,207 --> 00:21:30,917
Goblin #3: YUMMY.
LET’S TIE ’EM TO THE OTHER ONE.

457
00:21:30,917 --> 00:21:32,417
( both laugh )

458
00:21:32,417 --> 00:21:34,047
Goblin #4: SILENCE!

459
00:21:34,047 --> 00:21:36,887
THEY’RE MALE IUMS.

460
00:21:36,887 --> 00:21:39,637
WE TAKE ’EM BACK,
NO ONE BUY ’EM.

461
00:21:39,637 --> 00:21:43,097
WORTHLESS. KILL ’EM,
AND MAKE ’EM MEAT INSTEAD.

462
00:21:43,097 --> 00:21:45,307
( goblins chuckling )

463
00:21:45,307 --> 00:21:47,347
Kirito: EUGEO.

464
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:50,017
( Eugeo gasping )

465
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:51,607
